<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6685" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capsārĭus</span></b> , ii,
			m.
		capsa. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A slave who carried the satchels of boys going to
				school</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 40,
				2, 13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The maker of satchels</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 50, 6,
				6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A slave who took care of the clothes in baths</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Dig. 1, 15, 3, § 5</span></i>; Edict.
			Dom. p. 22.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>